For Exercise 1.16, I deployed the FastAPI inference service from my Fashion-MNIST MLOps project to Render using the Docker image I previously published to Docker Hub.

Docker Hub image: dbr007/fashion-mnist-api:v1

I created a Render Web Service using the existing Docker image, selected the Free compute plan, configured port 8000, and set /health as the health-check endpoint.

Render successfully pulled the image, started the FastAPI application using Uvicorn, and made the service publicly accessible through HTTPS.

The deployment logs confirmed successful application startup and HTTP 200 responses from the /health endpoint.

The root URL returns HTTP 404 because no root endpoint is defined. The application is accessible through its documented API routes.

The standalone inference service does not currently have a configured model artifact, so prediction readiness requires additional infrastructure.

